libipa: sensor helpers for the IMX682 and the S5K3T2 of the Xiaomi POCO X3 NFC

Without a helper, libcamera warns

    IPASoft: Failed to create camera sensor helper for imx682
    IPASoft: Failed to create camera sensor helper for s5k3t2

and automatic exposure control is left with the fallback branch in
soft_simple.cpp, which uses the register CODE as if it were the gain:

    context_.configuration.agc.againMax     = againMax;    /* 978 */
    context_.configuration.agc.again10      = againDef;    /* 0   */
    context_.configuration.agc.againMin     = againMin;    /* 0   */
    context_.configuration.agc.againMinStep = 1.0;

ON THE IMX682 THAT IS VERY WRONG, because its gain is not linear:

    gain = 1024 / (1024 - code)

that is, code 512 is 2x and 978 is 22.3x. Treating the axis as linear from 0 to
978 makes the automatic control believe it is moving by 0.1% at the top end,
where one step of code is worth almost 2% of gain. With the helper the AGC gets
the real range, 1x to 22.3x, and a proportionate step.

ON THE S5K3T2 THE FALLBACK BRANCH ALMOST GETS IT RIGHT, and that is worth
saying: its gain really is linear and passes through zero -code / 32-, and its
default value is exactly 32, so the AGC's relative arithmetic works out even
though the numbers are scaled. It is added anyway because it is correct and
because the helper is the place where that piece of data lives.

WHERE THE CONSTANTS COME FROM

Not from a datasheet I do not have, but from what the drivers themselves
declare, which is verifiable:

    imx682   min 0    max 978   default 0     -> 0 is 1x  ->  Sony 1024/(1024-x)
    s5k3t2   min 32   max 512   default 32    -> 32 is 1x ->  linear x/32

The black level of the imx682 is MEASURED on the sensor: with the scene in the
dark the image floor lands at 62..68 of ten bits, that is, the pedestal of 64,
which on the helper's 16-bit scale is 4096. It is the same value and the same
family as the imx708, which is already in this file.

The black level of the s5k3t2 is measured too, and by the same method: with the
exposure at its minimum -eight lines- the floor lands at 62..65 of ten bits, and
the long-exposure capture rises to a median of 253, which proves that the
control was being applied. They are the same 64 as the Sony.

The method does not require covering the camera: with the exposure at its
minimum the signal is negligible even if the scene is lit, and what is left is
the pedestal.
--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
@@ -654,6 +654,27 @@
 };
 REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("imx678", CameraSensorHelperImx678)
 
+class CameraSensorHelperImx682 : public CameraSensorHelper
+{
+public:
+	CameraSensorHelperImx682()
+	{
+		/*
+		 * Sony de diez bits, la misma familia que el imx708: el nivel de
+		 * negro es el pedestal de 64, y medido en el sensor del surya con
+		 * la escena a oscuras el suelo cae en 62..68 de diez bits.
+		 */
+		blackLevel_ = 4096;
+		/*
+		 * ganancia = 1024 / (1024 - codigo), la curva clasica de Sony.
+		 * El driver declara el rango 0..978, y el 0 como valor por
+		 * defecto: 1024/1024 = 1x abajo y 1024/46 = 22,3x arriba.
+		 */
+		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 0, 1024, -1, 1024 };
+	}
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("imx682", CameraSensorHelperImx682)
+
 class CameraSensorHelperImx708 : public CameraSensorHelper
 {
 public:
@@ -827,6 +848,29 @@
 };
 REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("ov13858", CameraSensorHelperOv13858)
 
+class CameraSensorHelperS5k3t2 : public CameraSensorHelper
+{
+public:
+	CameraSensorHelperS5k3t2()
+	{
+		/*
+		 * Pedestal de 64 en diez bits, MEDIDO en este sensor: con la
+		 * exposicion en su minimo el suelo cae en 62..65, y la captura de
+		 * exposicion larga sube a 253 de mediana, o sea que el mando hace
+		 * algo y la medida vale.
+		 */
+		blackLevel_ = 4096;
+		/*
+		 * Samsung con ganancia LINEAL: ganancia = codigo / 32. El propio
+		 * driver lo dice sin ambiguedad, porque declara el minimo Y el
+		 * valor por defecto en 32, que es donde un sensor esta a 1x, y el
+		 * maximo en 512, o sea 16x.
+		 */
+		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 1, 0, 0, 32 };
+	}
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("s5k3t2", CameraSensorHelperS5k3t2)
+
